</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Shenk</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tabor</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Varmus</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wimmer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Uncensored exchange of scientific results</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2003</year><volume>100</volume><fpage>1464</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12590129</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.0630491100</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B3"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cozzarelli</surname><given-names>NR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Unfettered access to published results</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2001</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>8159</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11447298</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.171309098</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B4"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cozzarelli</surname><given-names>NR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>For free access, follow the brick red buttons</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2001</year><volume>292</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11294212</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.292.5514.51c</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Luttich</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sclabas</surname><given-names>G M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Frequently asked questions about Molecular Cancer</article-title><source>Mol C